  "body": "## What changed\n\nA cross drill on a lathe or a mill-turn now has a first-traverse law. Generation refuses a cross drill by name if its first rapid from the turret's index position can pass the work or the steel.\n\n- **Premise.** The unknown start is the turret's index position, at the top of the X and Z travel. This is the premise of #2987 and of the upright law. A program that starts with the tool low near the work (for example after a manual jog) is not covered. The decision file says so.\n- **The post's real first move.** `fanuc-lathe.cps` `liveMove` (lines 717-720) writes `G00 C`, then `G00 X Z` to the first motion record. The record stream writes the END of each move only (`crates/post/src/post/mod.rs:532-536`). The start of the first move goes out only as `StartX/Y/Z` (`mod.rs:274-280`), and `liveMove` does not move there. So the first G00 X Z goes to the R-plane point of the first hole.\n- **The law** (`camcraft_sim::verify::live_first_traverse`, `crates/sim/src/verify/live_traverse.rs`).\n  - A G00 moves each axis at its own rate. Thus the tip can pass every radius from the first point out, at every Z from the first point up, in the station's plane.\n  - The tool lies along the radius. The swept solid follows the tool stack: flute, then shank, then holder, the widest band so far.\n  - The work and the chuck are read at the C angle: each facet is clipped exactly.\n  - Fixed steel (a tailstock, the table) is read revolved about the spindle.\n  - A face that only touches the swept solid passes. The model excess follows the #1053 law.\n- **Seam.** `crates/app/src/operation/cross_traverse.rs` is called in the cross branch of `generate.rs`. A hit gives `GenError::Invalid` with the solid's name, so nothing posts. A mill-turn cross drill also answers to the upright law, because its default post is the mill post.\n- **Cache.** The cross drill's op stamp gets the word `live-traverse-3077`.\n- **One test fixture changed** (coordinator decision, recorded in the decision file).\n  - In `drilling_cross::recognition_finds_the_bar_two_holes_and_they_generate`, the 44 mm box stock stands out to X 22 from Z 0 up. At clearance 20, the first hole's R plane is at radius 20, Z -10. The first rapid's Z leg passes 2 mm of uncut stock, so the law refuses it correctly.\n  - The test's clearance is now 30, which puts the R plane at radius 30. The test still pins the recognition and the generation.\n  - Dropped: a rule that this stock is not there.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3077-lathe-cross-first-traverse.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Example refusal: \"the stock reaches out to 22.000 from the spindle at Z0.000\" (the old recognition fixture).\n- `coarse_cross_drill`: a flange flush with the R plane (x 20) is clear. Earlier drafts refused it.\n- `drilling_cross_box`: the Ø12 shank stands 30 mm behind the tip and does not meet a lump 3 mm beside the drill's line. An earlier draft refused it.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/lathe_cross_drill.rs`:\n  - `a_cross_drill_over_its_chuck_has_a_clear_first_traverse`\n  - `a_cross_drill_under_a_wide_tailstock_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `a_thin_tailstock_centre_is_clear_on_a_lathe_and_convicts_a_mill_turn`\n  - `a_turning_collar_flush_with_the_first_point_is_clear_and_one_proud_of_it_is_refused`\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/live_traverse_tests.rs`: 9 unit tests (tool width, touch, #1053 excess, shank band, half-plane, square bar, clipped facet, spindle off origin, unreadable input).\n\n## Quick gate (local, debug)\n\n- camcraft-sim lib `live_traverse`: 9 of 9 pass.\n- camcraft-app on the final head: `drilling_cross` (9), `coarse_cross_drill` (6), `lathe_cross_drill` (9), `drilling_cross_box` (7) pass.\n- camcraft-app on `37a84a2b5` (before the #1053 excess change and the fixture change): these binaries pass:\n  - `cross_drill_neighbours`, `drill_reach`\n  - `drilling_cross_holder`, `drilling_cross_part`, `drilling_cross_spindle`, `drilling_cross_stock`\n  - `first_traverse_rotary`, `lathe_post`, `lathe_work_spindle`, `stock_source_cross_drill`\n- The later changes apply the excess only when the model has one, and they change one test case.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Heavy lanes: not run, covered by the cut gate.\n- The `operations` suite was not run on this head.\n- The turret body is not modelled.\n- The other mill-turn kinds stay outside this law (#3083).\n\nNote: PR #3093 (#3081) also changes `crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse.rs`. This PR does not change that file. It changes the call at the upright judge in `generate.rs`.\n\nChangelog: A cross drill on a lathe or a mill-turn is refused by name when its first rapid from the turret's index position can pass the stock, a part, a chuck or a tailstock.\n\nEffort: max (escalated from high)\n\nFixes #3077\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
